course: dictionary
lesson: 4510
title: Small word, big job: he
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «He» is a pronoun. A pronoun is a little word that stands in for a name, so we do not keep repeating it. «Tom is late. He missed the bus.» Here «he» points back to Tom, the boy already named.
explain: «He» is the subject of a sentence: it tells you who does the action. «He kicked the ball» means he is the one doing the kicking. Other forms change: «him» is used when he receives the action, as in «I saw him», «his» shows ownership, as in «his coat», and «himself» is used when he does something to himself.
explain: Use the earlier words to find who «he» means. «Tariq's dad drives him there and picks him up at nine.» Here «him» means Tariq, the boy being driven and collected. Ask yourself: who is this word pointing back to? The answer is always somewhere earlier in the text.
fact: «He» points back to a boy, man or male animal who has already been named.
fact: «He» is the subject of a sentence, so it usually comes before the action word: «He runs fast.»
fact: «He'll» means he will, «he'd» means he would or he had, and «he's» means he is or he has.
fact: «He» can also mean any person when we do not know who, but today «they» is more common.
fact: A «he» is an informal word for a male animal or person: «Is the puppy a he or a she?»
exercise: «Tom is one of two mates. He still says hi in the corridor.» Who does «he» point back to? | The other mate, who is a girl | The teacher | The corridor | *Tom
exercise: «The King said the Cat could kiss ___ hand.» Which word fits the gap? | he | him | himself | *his
exercise: In «he'll be here soon», what does he'll mean? | *he will | he would | he was | he has
test: «Tariq's dad picks him up at nine.» Who is him? | The dad | The car | *Tariq | The school
test: Which word fits? «___ bag is red.» (The boy owns the bag.) | Himself | He | *His | Him
exam: In «He lived by the sea», which word tells us who does the action? | The sea | Lived | By | *He
